{"id": "section-body-03117", "title": "Cholera", "chapterId": "chapter-four", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "NOTIFIABLE DISEASES", "Bacterial Infections", "Cholera"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-03117", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Cholera", "runs": [{"text": "Cholera"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1802"}}, {"id": "body-03118", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Cholera is an acute gastrointestinal infection caused by Vibrio cholerae. Infection occurs through ingestion of contaminated water or food by Vibrio cholerae leading to severe diarrhoea and emesis associated with body fluid and electrolyte depletion.", "runs": [{"text": "Cholera is an acute gastrointestinal infection caused by Vibrio cholerae. Infection occurs through ingestion of contaminated water"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "food"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Vibrio"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cholerae"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "leading"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "severe"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "diarrhoea"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "emesis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "associated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "body"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fluid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "electrolyte"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "depletion."}]}, {"id": "body-03119-textbox1-00001", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Note: When a case of cholera is suspected at home, advise to rehydrate the patient using ORS if available while preparing to take the patient to the nearest health facility or Cholera Treatment Centre", "runs": [{"text": "Note:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "When"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cholera"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "suspected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "at"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "home,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "advise"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rehydrate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "using"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ORS"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "if"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "available"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "while"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "preparing to take the patient to the nearest health facility or Cholera Treatment Centre"}]}, {"id": "body-03121", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-03122", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A sudden onset of painless watery diarrhoea that may quickly become severe with profuse watery stool, vomiting, severe dehydration and muscular cramps, leading to hypovolemic shock and death", "runs": [{"text": "A sudden onset of painless watery diarrhoea that may quickly become severe with profuse watery stool, vomiting, severe"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dehydration and muscular cramps, leading to hypovolemic shock and death"}]}, {"id": "body-03124", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Case Definition", "runs": [{"text": "Case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Definition"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-03125", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Suspected cholera case: In areas where a cholera outbreak has not been declared: Any patient aged two years and older presenting with acute watery diarrhoea and severe dehydration or dying from acute watery diarrhoea", "runs": [{"text": "Suspected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cholera"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "case:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "In"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "areas"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "where"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {